---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const focus = [
  { title: 'Reflective Journaling', body: '23 er Diary — identity, memory, self-awareness.' },
  { title: 'Technical Documentation', body: 'Turning defect reports and architecture notes into clear knowledge bases.' },
  { title: 'Essays', body: 'Shorter pieces on QA, product thinking, and the psychology of systems.' },
];
---
<Layout title="Writer — Wahidul Alam Nahid">

  <div class="draft-banner">⚠ Draft copy — written to match tone/structure, needs Wahid's real voice before publishing</div>

  <header class="persona-hero" style="--accent: var(--mustard);">
    <div class="disc-solo"></div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="kicker" style="color:var(--mustard);">Section 02 — Writer</span>
      <h1>I write to understand, not to impress.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Writing is where I put the QA instinct and the personal instinct in the same room — precise where it needs to be, honest everywhere else.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="persona-body" style="--accent: var(--mustard);">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="persona-copy">
        <p>A defect report and a diary entry aren't as different as they sound. Both start with an observation, ask what actually happened versus what was supposed to happen, and refuse to move on until the gap is named honestly.</p>
        <p><em>23 er Diary</em> is where that habit runs without a ticket number attached — pages on memory, identity, and the version of myself I was a year ago versus now. It's less a public blog than a working record, the same way test logs are a working record of a system's honesty.</p>
        <p>The rest of the writing is more practical: documentation that turns a tangle of architecture decisions into something a new teammate can actually follow, and essays that try to do the same for less technical questions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="focus-grid">
        <span class="kicker" style="color:var(--mustard);">Focus Areas</span>
        {focus.map((f) => (
          <div class="focus-card" style="--accent: var(--mustard);">
            <h3>{f.title}</h3>
            <p>{f.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="novel-callout">
        <span class="novel-sub">Currently Writing</span>
        <div class="novel-cover"><img src="/images/avyantar-cover.jpg" alt="Avyantar — illustration of a man looking out a window at a passing train" /></div>
        <div style="text-align:center;max-width:60ch;margin:0 auto;">
          <h3 lang="bn">অভ্যন্তর <span lang="en" style="font-family:var(--body);font-weight:500;color:var(--ink-soft);">(Avyantar — "Inside")</span></h3>
          <p>A serialized Bengali-language novel-in-progress — a psychological journey following Shofique/Anis, where memory, isolation, and an unraveling sense of self blur the line between reality and delusion. Twelve chapters are planned; the first is written.</p>
          <blockquote lang="bn" style="text-align:left;">অভ্যন্তর — শূন্যতা, স্মৃতি, ট্রেনের ঝকঝকে শব্দ আর ভেতরের অজানা সত্তার লড়াই। ১২টি অধ্যায়ে unfold হয় শফিক/আনিসের গল্প—এক মানসিক যাত্রা যেখানে বাস্তব আর মায়ার সীমানা মিশে যায়।</blockquote>
          <a class="btn-ghost" href="/avyantar-ch1">Read Chapter 1 (Bengali) →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="back-link wrap"><a class="btn-ghost" href="/">← Back home</a></div>

</Layout>
